{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/shuffled()"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Inherited from ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sequence.shuffled()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"shuffled"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/shuffled()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"Swift","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"shuffled"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"externalID":"s:STsE8shuffledSay7ElementQzGyF::SYNTHESIZED::s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V","title":"shuffled()","modules":[{"relatedModules":["Swift"],"name":"Cliques"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method"},"references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques","title":"Cliques","abstract":[]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/shuffled()":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/shuffled()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/shuffled()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"shuffled","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","title":"shuffled()","role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"MaximalCliques"}}}